INFERENCE WEEKLY - BULLETIN
Tuesday, March 10, 2026, 11:30am Pacific

A short one outside the usual Friday slot because a lot of you are affected.

One of the three frontier API providers has been returning elevated error rates since about 8:40am Pacific. Readers report 30-70% of requests failing with 5xx errors across all model tiers; the batch tier appears unaffected because it is queued. The provider's status page moved from "investigating" to "identified" at 10:15 and says a fix is rolling out region by region. No cause has been given.

What teams are doing, from the replies so far:
- Those with a routing gateway in front of the API flipped a fallback to a second provider within minutes and are mostly fine, at a higher cost per token.
- Those calling the API directly are either retrying with backoff and eating the latency or have degraded the feature.
- Two teams discovered that their fallback path had never been tested and does not work. Both are fixing it live.

If you have a fallback configured, now is when you learn whether it works. If you do not, the cheapest insurance is a gateway with a second provider key, and it takes an afternoon.

We will have the full picture and the provider's post-mortem in Friday's issue. Reply with your experience; anonymized reports help everyone.

